Release a leaked group reference and validate directory entries

Backports from gkostka/lwext4, library parts only, byte for byte (their
tests are not carried):

- PR #118, commit 5004e9527cda1d5a0b2d88aa33c262bce37efd0b (Christopher
  Thomas): ext4_ialloc_free_inode() released neither the block group
  reference nor the descriptor block when reading the inode bitmap
  failed, and ext4_ialloc_alloc_inode() ignored the results of
  ext4_block_set() and ext4_fs_put_block_group_ref().  Fixes lwext4
  issue #57.
- PR #112, commit 35a8dde0ff281d860e8f96b632147b2b4b51f69e (Christopher
  Thomas): ext4_dir_entry_next() dereferenced a NULL entry for a
  directory with no entries (lwext4 issue #89, CVE-2025-70099).
  ext4_dir_en_is_valid(), modelled on Linux __ext4_check_dir_entry(),
  now checks every entry in the iterator, ext4_dir_find_in_block() and
  ext4_dir_try_insert_entry(): find_in_block() could read past the
  block buffer, and try_insert_entry() looped forever on a zero rec_len
  or wrote an entry with an underflowed length.  Directory holes are
  skipped, and ext4_dir_iterator_init() releases its block on failure.

Applies after 0002.

